# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  WHAT DOES NOT GET DEPLOYED
#
#  The repository is the site: Vercel serves every file in it, at its path,
#  to anyone. That is fine for HTML, CSS, JS and photos. It was not fine for
#  everything else that happens to live here.
#
#  Before this file, all of these answered 200 to a stranger:
#
#      supabase/access-control.sql   47KB — 261 email addresses, each with the
#                                    person's role and which department they
#                                    are scoped to. The access list itself.
#      supabase/seed.sql             170KB — employees, KPIs, OKRs, the org
#                                    chart. Every row the hub renders.
#      supabase/schema.sql           25KB — table definitions, views, and the
#                                    row-level security policies, which is a
#                                    map of exactly where the doors are.
#      supabase/*.py                 the provisioning scripts.
#
#  So the row-level security in supabase/rls-lockdown.sql was being handed
#  back in full by the deploy. Locking the database while publishing the seed
#  file is not locking anything.
#
#  These stay in git — they are how the database is built and reviewed. They
#  simply stop being part of what the web server can hand out.
#
#  ── After deploying, check it ──
#
#      curl -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' https://<site>/supabase/seed.sql
#
#  Expect 404. A 200 means this file is not being applied and the SQL is still
#  public.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Everything that builds or describes the database. None of it is ever fetched
# by a page.
supabase/

# Documentation and editor state.
README.md
docs/
.vscode/
.claude/

# Spreadsheets the provisioning scripts read. Kept out by pattern as well as by
# name: "Hub Access List.xlsx" is the access list in its original form, and the
# next one to land here should not have to be remembered.
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.csv

# Screenshots kept for reference rather than served by any page.
dashboard-screenshots/
